# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  InsightPulse AI — FRONTEND PRODUCTION (Vercel)
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  Vite auto-loads this file during `vite build`, so committing it means Vercel
#  builds correctly with nothing configured in the dashboard. You can still
#  override it in Vercel -> Settings -> Environment Variables.
#
#  Root Directory on Vercel must be `frontend`, otherwise vercel.json is not
#  picked up and a hard refresh on /app/overview returns 404.
#
#  Nothing secret belongs in this file. Every VITE_* variable is inlined into
#  the browser bundle at build time and is therefore public. Provider API keys
#  stay on the backend.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# The backend's PUBLIC Railway domain.
#
# Must NOT be https://insightpulse-ai.railway.internal — that is Railway's
# private IPv6 network, which only resolves between services inside the same
# Railway project. A browser cannot reach it, so the site would load but every
# API call would fail with ERR_NAME_NOT_RESOLVED and the dashboard would sit on
# "Backend offline".
#
# No trailing slash. Vite inlines this at BUILD time, so changing it needs a
# redeploy, not just a restart.
VITE_API_BASE=https://insightpulse-ai-production.up.railway.app
